INT. SUBWAY CAR - EVENING

The train is very full and it is hot and a man named Ivo, 30s, with a blue bag between his feet, holds the pole with one hand and looks at the floor while a girl, Dasha, 20s, is pressed against him by the crowd and tries to read her phone over a shoulder, and at the far end of the car a thin man in a grey coat, Pavel, 40s, watches them both and does not look at anything else.

ON PHONE: Dasha - where r u

Dasha types with one thumb. She looks up. Ivo looks away.

ON PHONE: Dasha - i see u. wave

Ivo does not wave. His knuckles are white on the pole.

DASHA
(quiet)
You have what I need?

IVO
(quiet)
Not here.

The train brakes. Everybody leans together. Pavel moves two steps closer through the crowd, one hand in his coat pocket, and a woman with shopping bags says something sharp in another language that nobody answers.

DASHA
He is coming.

IVO
I know.

ON PHONE: Dasha - dont turn around

Ivo turns around. Pavel is very close now. The doors open. Nobody gets off.

PAVEL
(smiling)
You are in my seat, I think.

IVO
There is no seat.
